  "adaptations": [
    {
      "id": "tombs-secondary-class-generation",
      "note": "A dual-class (Tombs of Terror) run drafts from both classes, but the engine's Discover and random pools follow the primary class (Classes[0]) only. The exceptions are the explorer treasures' own class Discovers (ULDA_301 Map of Uldum, ULDA_303 Starseeker's Tools), which offer cards of both row classes (RunContext.PlayerClasses). Other Tombs secondary-class generation is not modelled."
    },
    {
      "id": "tombs-vip-membership-tavern",
      "note": "ULDA_011 VIP Membership ('Taverns you visit are upgraded!', phase 6 F13): the client data does not say what an upgraded tavern is (the original was server-side). In SoloStone an upgraded tavern gives 1 more gold and offers 1 more option (DungeonRun.VipExtraGold, DungeonRun.VipExtraOffers); the treasure has no match effect."
    }
  ],
  "exclusionNotes": {
  },
  "customBucketsAbout": "Phase 6 (F16): themed SoloStone-curated pool entries for the classes no original adventure offered (Death Knight, Demon Hunter), so an act run's fourteen drafts never run dry under any pick order (seven entries each; the phase 6 review walked always-pick-last runs that fell to 2 offers on floors 13-14 with four. The Death Knight entries share cards, as the rune-free Death Knight cards admitted are few). Members are admitted, scripted, rune-free collectible cards of the class (the catalog tool fails the build on any other); each entry is taken at most draft.bucketMaxTakes times.",
